title: 'sp-api: Allow runtime API parameters to opt into EncodeLike'

doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Parameters of a runtime API are forwarded to the runtime as SCALE bytes, so the client side
    does not need the declared type, only something that encodes to the same bytes. A parameter of
    a trait declared with `decl_runtime_apis!` can now be marked with `#[encode_like]`, which makes
    the generated client side method generic over `parity_scale_codec::EncodeLike<DeclaredType>`
    for that parameter. Callers can then pass a value they already hold instead of converting it
    first.

    The marker is opt in per parameter, because a generic parameter cannot be inferred at the call
    site: expressions such as `value.into()`, `None` or `vec![]` would have to be named explicitly.
    Unmarked parameters keep their declared type, so existing call sites and their type inference
    are unaffected.

    `Core::execute_block` and `BlockBuilder::check_inherents` take their block parameter this way.
    Both declare `Block::LazyBlock`, which has the same encoding as `Block`, so callers holding a
    `Block` no longer have to convert it with `.into()` first.

    Only the client side is affected. The runtime side decodes the parameter into the declared
    type, so `impl_runtime_apis!` is unchanged. A mock does not see the declaration, so
    `mock_impl_runtime_apis!` requires the `#[encode_like]` marker to be repeated on the same
    parameter; the value is decoded back into the declared type before the body of the mock runs.

crates:
# The generated client side signature of `Core::execute_block` and `BlockBuilder::check_inherents`
# gained a generic parameter. Any caller that passes the declared type keeps compiling, so
# `validate: false`.
- name: sp-api
  bump: major
  validate: false
- name: sp-api-proc-macro
  bump: patch
- name: sp-block-builder
  bump: major
  validate: false
# Crates that only dropped a now unnecessary conversion at their call sites.
- name: sc-service
  bump: none
- name: sc-storage-chain-sync
  bump: none
- name: sc-rpc
  bump: none
- name: sc-basic-authorship
  bump: none
- name: sc-tracing
  bump: none
- name: frame-benchmarking-cli
  bump: none
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-aura
  bump: none
- name: cumulus-client-service
  bump: none
- name: cumulus-pallet-parachain-system
  bump: none
